Design for Component Recovery is a product design approach that prioritises the simplicity of retrieving and reutilizing components when a product reaches the end of its lifespan. The process includes the careful selection of long-lasting materials, the creation of products with interchangeable parts for convenient replacement or enhancement, and the guarantee that items may be disassembled without causing harm to the components. This method also incorporates the standardisation of components across various products to ease interchangeability and retrieval. Precise identification of components for material composition and recycling instructions is also a crucial factor. The DfCR approach adheres to circular design principles, which effectively reduce waste and preserve resources. Additionally, it has the potential to attract environmentally concerned consumers in the market.